                "annotations": [],
                "text": "Analyse the rule:\nEach contiguous rectangular block of non-zero color is hollowed out: its border remains, and its interior is filled with 0.\nSpecifically, for any rectangular shape of color $C \\ne 0$, pixels that are strictly inside the rectangle (i.e. not on its top, bottom, left, or right edges) become 0.\n\nWait, are they always rectangles?\nIn example 2:\n- 7: 5x8 rectangle from (1,6) to (5,13). Hollowed out: interior (2..4, 7..12) becomes 0.\n- 8: 5x5 rectangle from (7,11) to (11,15). Hollowed out: interior (8..10, 12..14) becomes 0.\n- 1: 8x4 rectangle from (8,1) to (15,4). Hollowed out: interior (9..14, 2..3) becomes 0.\n- 2: 3x3 rectangle from (13,9) to (15,11). Hollowed out: interior (14,10) becomes 0.\n- 9: 3x6 rectangle from (14,13) to (16,18). Hollowed out: interior (15, 14..17) becomes 0.\n\nSo every solid rectangle of non-zero color has its interior set to 0.\n\nReady for test input. Please provide the test input.",
